  "residualRisks": [
    {
      "id": "R-SECURE-PARAMETERS",
      "text": "Secure parameter values (RevenueCat key and webhook authorization, Entra client secret) are never read by the gate and what-if cannot compare them. The deploying shell must export the SAME values production has: a wrong RevenueCat value breaks purchases. Check them with verify-secure-parameters.sh before you approve."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-MYSQL-ADMIN-PASSWORD",
      "text": "The MySQL administrator password is not part of any deployment (the server is left alone). Azure never returns it and the gate cannot verify it. It is changed only out of band, and both APIs read it from Key Vault: a change has to update the secret and restart the apps in the same step, neither of which the gate checks. A server that is created (mode create) gets its password from a secure parameter that cannot be compared."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-RESTART",
      "text": "Writing app settings restarts the affected apps. Expect a short interruption (cold start) on every deployment that touches a settings bag."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-KV-SECRETS",
      "text": "Key Vault secret names and values are not verified: the vault is private and the gate never reads secrets. A reference to a missing secret only shows up when the app starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-WHATIF-LIMITS",
      "text": "what-if cannot read app settings, siteConfig details or guid()-named role assignments. The gate covers names and structure from live read-only listings; it does not prove that secret values are right."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-OUTSIDE-ARM",
      "text": "Cloudflare, GitHub, Entra app registrations and MySQL users are outside Azure Resource Manager and are not checked."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-DRIFT-WINDOW",
      "text": "Production can change between the gate run and the deployment. The evidence expires after 30 minutes; run the gate again if you wait longer."
    }
  ],
